		{
			"id": "110984938338243414",
			"parentId": "110984915662339438",
			"url": "https://mstdn.social/@mattwilcox/110984938085720195",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matt Wilcox",
				"url": "https://mstdn.social/@mattwilcox",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/287/949/593/182/322/original/ea34d8a24964f103.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-31T15:29:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@sarajw\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sarajw</span></a></span> This is the trouble with getting into the whole contrast area of thought: there is no \"one good design\". For some people, whatever you do it's too high contrast, too low contrast, too much glare, etc etc. Heck even the color contrast algo in the a11y criteria is wonky compared with how most people see colours. <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110984944085290528",
			"parentId": "110984938338243414",
			"url": "https://mstdn.social/@mattwilcox/110984943937919537",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matt Wilcox",
				"url": "https://mstdn.social/@mattwilcox",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/287/949/593/182/322/original/ea34d8a24964f103.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-31T15:30:48.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@sarajw\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sarajw</span></a></span> (I also happen to think a lot of the preferences depends on the literal physical context of where people are sitting looking at screens, which in turn depends on the time of day they do it, which direction the room and windows are facing, etc. It's all massively subjective.) <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
