			"date": "2023-08-31T15:52:51.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.social/@mattwilcox\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mattwilcox</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> no, I agree. Ravelry had terrible redesign backlash from people getting headaches, when moving from a lower contrast rounded edges design to something more angular and high contrast.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110985056715929506",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://toot.io/@synlogic/110985056663143698",
			"author": {
