			},
			"date": "2023-08-31T20:43:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@iamschulz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>iamschulz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://yatil.social/@yatil\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>yatil</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@hmig\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>hmig</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> yeah I think so! While being playful at the same time.</p><p>I know that my personal site main theme has some dodgy low contrast in places especially as each tab gets lighter in the dark mode version, that's why I decided to add a contrast toggle</p>",
